}

// WHAT A CONTAINER IMAGE CAN ACTUALLY RUN IS MEASURED INSIDE IT, ON THE ACCELERATOR IT WILL RUN ON.
//
// WHY THIS MODULE EXISTS. gunbc.spark.serving_arm carries one measured runtime property -- the
// architecture registry -- and that is enough to decide whether an engine will START. It is not
// enough to decide whether a checkpoint will RUN WELL, or at all, on a specific compute capability:
// DeepSeek V4.1 asks for an FP4 weight path, an FP4-quantised indexer KV cache, the V4.1 compressed
// sparse attention (CSA2) path and the DSpark speculator, and each of those is a separate body of
// kernels that an image either ships compiled for this SM or does not. An image can register the
// architecture and still be missing every one of them.
//
// THE UPSTREAM SOURCE IS NOT THE ANSWER, AND THIS IS THE WHOLE DISCIPLINE OF THIS MODULE. vLLM at
// 07b75534651a0dd584c6f3be75d8c62fb8426397 carries vllm/models/deepseek_v4_1/nvidia/model.py with an
// explicit SM12 branch, so the CODE exists upstream. Every image probed below is built from an
// earlier commit and ships none of it. Reading the upstream tree tells you what COULD be in an
// image; only executing inside the image tells you what IS.
//
// SO EVERY ROW HERE IS A RECEIPT OF AN EXECUTED PROBE, and an image nobody ran the probe in has no
// row -- it has a roster entry saying so, with the reason. The distinction is the point: a missing
// capability and an unasked question have different remedies, and fusing them is how a partial sweep
// comes to read as a complete one.

// ── THE SUBJECT: ONE EXACT IMAGE ON ONE EXACT COMPUTE CAPABILITY ───────────────────────────────
//
// Both halves are load-bearing. A digest without a compute capability is a claim about an image in
// general, and an image that ships sm_100 kernels answers differently on a GB200 than on a GB10; a
// compute capability without a digest is a claim about hardware that no engine can act on.
type ComputeCapability sole_constructor {
  major: Nat
  minor: Nat
}

fn compute_capability_label(c: ComputeCapability) -> String {
  join(["sm_", to_string(c.major), to_string(c.minor)], "")
}

// GB10, AS THE ACCELERATOR ITSELF REPORTS IT. `torch.cuda.get_device_capability(0)` returned (12, 1)
// inside every container probed below, on spark-a3ee, 2026-09-11. It is recorded here as a fleet
// OBSERVATION and not as a property of extdeps.systems.nvidia's GB10 catalog row, which deliberately
// leaves compute_capability none because the cited NVIDIA pages do not state it: an observation this
// repository made is a receipt in the observing layer, never a fact backfilled into the vendor's.
data gb10_observed_compute_capability: ComputeCapability = ComputeCapability { major: 12, minor: 1 }

type ProbedRuntimeImage sole_constructor {
  image_reference: NonEmptyStr
  framework: NonEmptyStr
  framework_version: NonEmptyStr
}

// ── THE CAPABILITIES, ONE PER BODY OF KERNELS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// These are not degrees of one capability and must not be collapsed into a score. An image with the
// architecture registered and no FP4 weight path is a different situation from one with the kernels
// and no registry entry: the first needs a checkpoint in another quantisation, the second needs a
// newer engine. A single "supported" Bool cannot distinguish them, which is the same defect that
// made `registers_glm5_next` unable to say anything about DeepSeek V4.1.
type RuntimeKernelCapability
  = ArchitectureRegistered
  | Fp4WeightKernels
  | Fp4KvCacheKernels
  | Csa2CompressorKernels
  | DSparkSpeculator

fn runtime_kernel_capability_label(c: RuntimeKernelCapability) -> String {
  match c {
    ArchitectureRegistered => "architecture-registered"
    Fp4WeightKernels => "fp4-weight-kernels"
    Fp4KvCacheKernels => "fp4-kv-cache-kernels"
    Csa2CompressorKernels => "csa2-compressor-kernels"
    DSparkSpeculator => "dspark-speculator"
  }
}

// ABSENT AND UNPROBEABLE ARE DIFFERENT ANSWERS. A capability the probe looked for and did not find
// is a measured negative that ranks the image out. A probe that could not execute -- no interpreter
// at the expected path, an image that will not start, a host with no accelerator -- establishes
// NOTHING about the image, and an arm that reported it as absent would turn a broken probe into
// evidence against a candidate that might be the right one.
type KernelProbeOutcome
  = KernelObservedPresent { symbol: NonEmptyStr }
  | KernelObservedAbsent { symbol: NonEmptyStr }
  | KernelProbeRefused { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type RuntimeCapabilityProbeRow {
  image: ProbedRuntimeImage
  host: NonEmptyStr
  compute_capability: ComputeCapability
  probed_at: NonEmptyStr
  capability: RuntimeKernelCapability
  outcome: KernelProbeOutcome
}


// ── THE ARCHITECTURE QUESTION IS DERIVED, NOT RESTATED ─────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Each probed image's registry reading -- the answer, the host, the date and the instrument -- lives
// in gunbc.spark.runtime_architecture_registry_reading, because it is a receipt this repository
// produced rather than anything the image's publisher declares. The ArchitectureRegistered rows
// below ask those readings rather than carrying a second hand-written answer: one reading per
// digest, one place it is written, and a row that cannot drift away from what it summarises.
//
// THE NAME BEING LOOKED FOR IS THE MODEL'S AUTHORITY, NOT THIS MODULE'S.
// extdeps.deepseek.deepseek_v4_1_flash owns `architectures[0]` of config.json at the pinned
// revision; spelling it again here would be a second authority for one fact, which is what this
// import exists to prevent.
fn architecture_registered_outcome(reading: ArchitectureRegistryReading) -> KernelProbeOutcome {
  if registry_reading_contains(r: reading, architecture: deepseek_v4_1_flash_architecture_class) {
    KernelObservedPresent { symbol: v41_probe_registry_symbol }
  } else {
    KernelObservedAbsent { symbol: v41_probe_registry_symbol }
  }
}

data v41_probe_registry_symbol: NonEmptyStr = "the image's own model registry, asked whether it answers for extdeps.deepseek.deepseek_v4_1_flash deepseek_v4_1_flash_architecture_class" as NonEmptyStr

// ── THE EXECUTED ROWS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Every row below was produced by one script executed inside the named digest on spark-a3ee with
// `docker run --gpus all` on 2026-09-11. The script imports the framework, loads the compiled
// operator libraries, reads the architecture registry, and then asks each capability question by
// its own symbol -- no capability is derived from another, so an image that registered the
// architecture but shipped no FP4 path would be recorded exactly that way.

